{
 "description": "3HDM-S3 scalar decay observables at general delta, the CP-even Higgs-basis angle (delta = -psi, the residual 2x2 block angle; the draft's total angle is alpha = theta_v + delta). VV couplings, predicted delta per benchmark point, and LFV Higgs branching ratios (tau mu, tau e, e mu) against the CMS limits.  Quark Yukawas are not part of this build, so BRs use the SM prediction for the total Higgs width (LHC Higgs XS WG).",
 "conventions": {
  "delta": "-psi with psi the residual CP-even 2x2 block angle; alpha = theta_v + delta. Scenario A is delta 0, B is pi/2, but |delta| < pi/4 always, so h_1 always carries the larger hVV coupling and B is a limit, not a reachable point.",
  "gamma_h_total_GeV": 0.0041,
  "lfv_limits": {
   "tau_mu_CMS21": 0.0015,
   "tau_e_CMS21": 0.0022,
   "e_mu_CMS23": 4.4e-05
  },
  "lepton_yukawa_split": "G_k read off the Lagrangian with all three VEVs symbolic (lfv.lepton_g_function). Supersedes the first version, whose sqrt3-typed-in M_l gave G_2 = 0 and a wrong Q_2 (h_0 couplings)."
 },
 "vv_couplings": {
  "h_1": "i g_w m_W cos(delta)",
  "h_0": "0 (exact, any delta)",
  "h_2": "i g_w m_W sin(delta)"
 },
